{
  "scene_id": "scene03_demystifying_the_model",
  "video_title": "What Is Machine Learning?",
  "scene_title": "Demystifying The Model",
  "order": 3,
  "duration_mode": "audio_driven",
  "voice": {
    "language": "en-IN",
    "speaker": "priya",
    "model": "bulbul:v3"
  },
  "narration": [
    {
      "id": "s3_01",
      "text": "One word comes up everywhere in machine learning: model."
    },
    {
      "id": "s3_02",
      "text": "That word can sound mysterious at first. But the idea is simple."
    },
    {
      "id": "s3_03",
      "text": "A model is a mathematical function. It takes an input, and it produces an output."
    },
    {
      "id": "s3_04",
      "text": "We usually write that as: x to y."
    },
    {
      "id": "s3_05",
      "text": "Or more formally: y equals f of x."
    },
    {
      "id": "s3_06",
      "text": "That is all a model is at the core."
    },
    {
      "id": "s3_07",
      "text": "For example, suppose we look at house prices."
    },
    {
      "id": "s3_08",
      "text": "On one axis, we plot house size. On the other, we plot price."
    },
    {
      "id": "s3_09",
      "text": "The points will not form a perfect line. Real data is messy."
    },
    {
      "id": "s3_10",
      "text": "But even in the mess, a pattern appears."
    },
    {
      "id": "s3_11",
      "text": "The model tries to capture that pattern."
    },
    {
      "id": "s3_12",
      "text": "So the model is not the data itself."
    },
    {
      "id": "s3_13",
      "text": "It is the structure the data suggests."
    },
    {
      "id": "s3_14",
      "text": "It is a compact mathematical summary of what the examples are telling us."
    },
    {
      "id": "s3_15",
      "text": "When we say a model is smart, we usually mean that it has learned parameters that make its predictions close to the real values."
    }
  ],
