  "notes": {
    "tone": "Calm, clean, and confidence-building. The scene should feel like the idea of a model is being gently unwrapped rather than announced with spectacle.",
    "pacing": "Keep the whole scene center-led with smooth transforms. The graph should emerge from the equation, and the fitted structure should remain after the raw points recede.",
    "animation_guidelines": "Prefer transform continuity over cut-like replacement. Keep one dominant focal object at each beat, avoid side layouts, and let the same centered plot evolve from axes to scatter to learned structure."
  }
